Original native Ezero integration

Ezero compiles through the original frontend, package initializer and runtime
into original Zero, then through the same Zero compiler. The native CLI runs
these stages in process and uses no subprocess compiler or foreign runtime.

Compose a frontend snapshot from authored parts:
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_FRONTEND.zero --ezero
The canonical source is ezero/compiler.zero. Composition preserves inputs and
refuses an existing destination. Build current host/guest artifacts with
zero-build PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY and verify language/file
behavior with zero-check PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_TEST_DIRECTORY.

See tools/compiler-cli.ztext for CLI layout, checks/README.ztext for native
verification, and ezero/README.ztext for the language. Earlier candidate
copies, overlay scripts and their build commands are no longer the workflow.
